# Dataset

The model is trained on [SSE-abacus](https://www.aissquare.com/datasets/detail?name=SSE-abacus&id=260&pageType=datasets) dataset, generated using the first-principles calculation software ABACUS (version 3.6.1). All data points are obtained using calculations based on the LCAO (Linear Combination of Atomic Orbitals) basis set. The entire dataset covers chalcogenide solid-state electrolytes, halide solid-state electrolytes, interface and some doped data.

# Parameters

The main parameters of training process include a batch size of 1, 1,000,000 steps, and the DPA-2 descriptor with cutoff radii (rcut) and selected numbers of neighbors (nsel) in the repinit layer and the repformer layer are 9.0 Å and 120, 4.0 Å and 40, respectively.

# Performances

||Energy RMSE (eV/atom)|Force RMSE (eV/Å)|
|-|-|-|
|Data std.|2.20E-01|6.98E-01|
|From scratch|1.40E-02|1.06E-01|

# Usage

One can use the following command to test the performance of the model in <test_system>.

```bash
dp --pt test -m SSE-ABACUS-dpa2.pt -s <test_system>
```


